  "projects": {
    "agent1-periodic-guarded-path": {
      "status": "PASS",
      "scope": "A supplied exact finite period-four quotient path with a natural copy schedule, literal exponent recurrence, and source guards k_i>=3 lifts an initial Canonical/full-column realization to the same ordinary seed through every endpoint. For any supplied initially original-valid finite path of length N, the literal recursive schedule starting at 2*N+3 supplies the guards and one positive canonical seed realizes all N steps. This formalizes the existing METHOD section4 finite-copy guard principle and reuses the original generic numeric representation theorem. The seed can depend on the path and N; no uniform infinite seed, safety, return existence, arbitrary abstract graph realization, affirmative interface search, or 196 conclusion.",
